notes.body:
@johnthacker I also thought you'd do a quick "performance check" to make sure startup didn't regress too much.
Some of the smil.dtd differences are just "list order" (which I'm guessing don't matter), but some of the attributes end up with different names (looking at the diff of the 2 provided files).  I still have the "debug" code that produces that output on a private branch if needed (was intended as a temporary hack with tshark using printfs).
Amended commits can certainly be made to this patch (especially if things like DTD file modification is required).  It's currently a draft so there is time to make edits.

